From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] settings: AD5X filament auto-refill; no-backup pop-up

Settings > Printer gets a "Filament Auto-Refill" row after Bed Heat Soak,
shown only where Klipper has the ifs object, with "On · Similar colour ·
backups for slot 1, 3" or "Off" as its second line. Its overlay has the
on/off switch (IFS_AUTO_REFILL ENABLE=), the colour match (Exact,
Similar, Any colour: IFS_AUTO_REFILL MATCH=), a live list of the slots
with filament, each with its colour swatch, material and the slots that
would take over (refill_backups with ifs_materials), a hint when no slot
has a backup, and "Filament slots", which opens the AMS panel where the
slots' materials and colours are set.

When a print loads a slot without a backup, Klipper sets refill_notice;
a "No backup spool" dialog then comes up on any screen during the print
(OK, Turn off auto-refill, Filament slots), once per distinct notice: a
reconnect does not bring the same one back, a new print (which clears
it) can. The print never waits for it. The model follows ifs and
ifs_materials from a new tail discovery step on; both objects join the
status subscription whenever Klipper has them.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
